[I] ROCm device libs

[T] ROCm device libs are the sources and CMake build of a set of AMD
[T] specific device-side language runtime libraries, provided as LLVM
[T] bitcode for OpenCL, HIP and OpenMP code compiled for AMD GPUs. They are
[T] part of AMD's LLVM fork.

[U] https://github.com/ROCm/llvm-project/

[A] Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[F] CROSS OBJDIR
[C] extra/development

[L] MIT
[V] 7.14.0
[P] X -----5---9 150.500

[CV-GROUP] rocm
[D] cf2f707886b78e24db0064fbbdd360b4bedc45003f25ee315963b813 llvm-project-rocm-7.14.0.tar.gz https://github.com/ROCm/llvm-project/archive/therock-7.14/

. $base/package/*/*/rocm-conf.in

srcdir=*/amd/device-libs
hook_add postmake 5 'sed -i s,$PWD/amdgcn,/$prefix/amdgcn, $root$libdir/cmake/AMDDeviceLibs/AMDDeviceLibsConfig.cmake'
